### 4. Add new Property-shaped scorer export (at end of file)
```diff
+import type { Property as PrismaProperty } from '@prisma/client';
+
+/**
+ * Calculate distress score directly from a Prisma Property row.
+ * Adapter for the tax-delinquent integration: virtual leads (Parcel+Lien) and
+ * promoted Properties both score from this entry point — no REAPI shape needed.
+ */
+export function calculateDistressScoreFromProperty(
+  p: Pick<PrismaProperty,
+    | 'foreclosure' | 'preForeclosure' | 'taxDelinquent' | 'vacant'
+    | 'bankruptcy' | 'absenteeOwner'
+    | 'estimatedValue' | 'assessedValue'
+    | 'taxDelinquentAmount' | 'taxDelinquentYearsCount' | 'taxDelinquentEarliestYear'
+  >
+): DistressScore {
+  // Adapt PrismaProperty → REAPIPropertyData shape
+  const adapted: Partial<REAPIPropertyData> = {
+    foreclosure: p.foreclosure,
+    preForeclosure: p.preForeclosure,
+    vacant: p.vacant,
+    absenteeOwner: p.absenteeOwner,
+    estimatedValue: p.estimatedValue ?? undefined,
+    // Tax-delinquent specific (the new path)
+    isTaxDelinquent: p.taxDelinquent,
+    taxDelinquentAmount: p.taxDelinquentAmount ?? undefined,
+    taxDelinquentYearsCount: p.taxDelinquentYearsCount ?? undefined,
+    taxDelinquentEarliestYear: p.taxDelinquentEarliestYear ?? undefined,
+  };
+  return calculateDistressScore(adapted as REAPIPropertyData);
+}
```

### Scoring math sanity check
| Scenario | Signals fired | Total | Grade | Motivation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Pure tax delinquent, $8k, 1yr (2024) | TAX_DELINQUENT(+20) | 20 | D | LOW |
| Tax delinquent, $94k, 3yr (2022-2024) | TAX_DELINQUENT(+20+5amt+5yrs+5deed=+30 capped) | 30 | D | LOW |
| Above + VACANT | TD(+30) + VACANT(+15) | 45 | C | MEDIUM |
| Above + OUT_OF_STATE | TD(+30) + VACANT(+15) + OOS(+15) | 60 | B | HIGH |
| Above + PRE_FORECLOSURE | +PRE_FC(+25) | 85 | A | HIGH |
| Max stack (TD+VACANT+OOS+LONG_TERM+HIGH_EQUITY+ABSENTEE+FREE_CLEAR) | 30+15+15+15+10+12+5 | 102 → capped 100 | A | HIGH |

Conclusion: TAX_DELINQUENT alone doesn't over-saturate (still Grade D), but stacks correctly with classical signals to reach Grade A. Cap math is safe.

